&lt;h2&gt;


🌷 Conclusão
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Estudar React permite compreender uma abordagem moderna para a construção de interfaces web.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Os conceitos de componentização, propriedades, gerenciamento de estado e renderização declarativa são fundamentais para desenvolver aplicações organizadas e escaláveis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mais importante do que memorizar a sintaxe é compreender o fluxo de dados, as responsabilidades dos componentes e a maneira como o React reage às mudanças de estado.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Com esses fundamentos, é possível avançar para assuntos como roteamento, gerenciamento de estado global, custom Hooks, consumo de APIs e otimização de desempenho.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


📚 Referências
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React — Official Documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/learn" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React — Quick Start&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://react.dev/reference/react/hooks" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React — Built-in Hooks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://vite.dev/guide/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Vite — Getting Started&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;dev.study — Anotações e estudos sobre desenvolvimento de software. ✨&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Your chat room component reconnects every time someone flips the dark-mode switch. Messages in flight get dropped, the "typing…" indicator resets, and support tickets call it "random." The bug isn't the dark-mode toggle — it's that &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; is sitting in a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; dependency array next to &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt;, and React has no way to know that only one of those two values should actually restart the connection.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reflex fix — deleting &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; from the array and silencing the lint warning — trades one bug for a worse one: the notification that fires on connect now shows whatever theme was active the moment the connection opened, forever, no matter how many times the user flips the switch afterward. That's a stale closure, and it's the single most common &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; bug there is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;React 19.2 (released October 1, 2025) shipped a real fix: the &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; Hook.&lt;/strong&gt; It lets an Effect read a value's &lt;em&gt;current&lt;/em&gt; state without that value forcing the Effect to re-run — something no combination of dependency-array tricks could do safely before. This article covers what &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; actually does, the exact rules for using it, and the one way people keep misusing it that makes things worse, not better.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This article is written against &lt;strong&gt;React 19.2+ / 19.3.0&lt;/strong&gt; (verified against the current npm &lt;code&gt;latest&lt;/code&gt; dist-tag for &lt;code&gt;react&lt;/code&gt; and cross-checked coverage of the official 19.2 release notes and the React docs' "Separating Events from Effects" guide; &lt;code&gt;react.dev&lt;/code&gt; itself was unreachable from this run's network, so claims here lean on the npm registry plus multiple independent write-ups of the same release). &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; requires React 19.2 or later and assumes React 19-era function components and hooks throughout.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What you'll learn
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By the end of this article you'll be able to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain the real difference between a value an Effect must &lt;em&gt;depend on&lt;/em&gt; and a value an Effect only needs to &lt;em&gt;read the latest copy of&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reproduce the stale-closure bug that "just remove it from the deps array" causes, and name why it happens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extract non-reactive logic out of an Effect with &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; and call it correctly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;List the hard rules — where it can be called, what it can't be passed to, why it's excluded from the dependency array — and what breaks if you ignore them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize when &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; is the wrong tool, because the value genuinely should resynchronize the Effect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Who this is for
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You've written a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; with a dependency array, you've seen the &lt;code&gt;react-hooks/exhaustive-deps&lt;/code&gt; lint warning, and you've been tempted to either silence it or just add everything it asks for. No class components or Server Components knowledge required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Table of contents
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The problem: one dependency array, two different jobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The mental model: reactive values vs. Effect Events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage 1 — the naive fix and its stale closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage 2 — useEffectEvent, correctly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stage 3 — more than one Effect Event&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edge cases and gotchas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FAQ&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cheat sheet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Key takeaways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The problem: one dependency array, two different jobs
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here's the chat room, written the obvious way:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ChatRoom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createConnection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showNotification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Connected!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome to &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;react-hooks/exhaustive-deps&lt;/code&gt; is doing its job here: the Effect reads both &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt;, so both are listed. The code is "correct" by the lint rule's own standard. It's also wrong in a way the lint rule has no way to catch, because the rule only knows one move — &lt;em&gt;list everything you read&lt;/em&gt; — and that move doesn't distinguish between two genuinely different jobs a value can have inside an Effect:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; decides what the Effect &lt;em&gt;does&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; A different room means a different connection. If &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; changes and the Effect doesn't re-run, you're connected to the wrong room. This is a &lt;strong&gt;reactive value&lt;/strong&gt; — the Effect's whole reason for existing is synchronized to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; is only &lt;em&gt;read&lt;/em&gt; once the connection is already open&lt;/strong&gt;, to decide what the notification looks like. It has no bearing on which room you connect to. Listing it as a dependency doesn't make the code more correct — it makes the Effect re-run (disconnect, then reconnect) for a reason that has nothing to do with what the Effect is for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Toggle dark mode in this version and the user drops their connection. Not because anything about the connection needed to change — because the lint rule, correctly, cannot tell the difference between "this value controls what the Effect synchronizes with" and "this value is read once a thing the Effect already started happens to fire."&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The mental model: reactive values vs. Effect Events
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The mental model:&lt;/strong&gt; a &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; dependency array isn't a list of "everything this function touches" — it's a list of &lt;strong&gt;reactive values the Effect's job depends on&lt;/strong&gt;. If a value changing should legitimately restart what the Effect is doing, it belongs in the array, full stop; that's not a style choice, it's correctness. But some reads inside an Effect aren't about &lt;em&gt;what the Effect is doing&lt;/em&gt; at all — they're about &lt;em&gt;what to do when something the Effect already set up happens later&lt;/em&gt;. React 19.2 gives that second category a name — an &lt;strong&gt;Effect Event&lt;/strong&gt; — and a Hook to create one: &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An Effect Event is a function, declared with &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent(fn)&lt;/code&gt;, whose body is deliberately &lt;strong&gt;non-reactive&lt;/strong&gt;: every time your component re-renders, React relinks the function to that render's latest props and state, but the function itself is never a dependency and never forces anything to re-run. You call it &lt;em&gt;from inside&lt;/em&gt; an Effect (or from inside another Effect Event) when the thing it does should happen using &lt;strong&gt;whatever is current right now&lt;/strong&gt;, not whatever was current when the Effect last ran.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Put plainly: &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; answers "what should this Effect be connected to?" — that's reactive, and it belongs in the array. &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; answers "what should happen, using today's value, when the thing I already connected to does something?" — that's an Effect Event, and it has no business in the array at all.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Stage 1 — the naive fix and its stale closure
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; existed, the common workaround was to simply drop &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; from the array and disable the lint rule:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ChatRoom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createConnection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// theme is captured from THIS render, forever, until roomId changes again&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showNotification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Connected!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps -- intentionally wrong, see below&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome to &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;This stops the reconnect. It also freezes &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; at whatever it was the moment the Effect last ran. JavaScript closures capture variables by reference to the scope they were created in, not by re-reading them later — so the &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; inside &lt;code&gt;connection.on("connected", …)&lt;/code&gt; is the one value from the render that created this particular closure. Flip dark mode ten times after that; the notification keeps showing the old theme until &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; changes and the whole Effect reruns. That's the stale closure: the code looks like it reads &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt;, but it's reading a frozen copy from the past.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the trap of "just remove it from the deps array and silence the warning": you've fixed the symptom (unwanted reconnects) by reintroducing the exact class of bug the lint rule exists to prevent (stale reads), just somewhere the rule can no longer see it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Stage 2 — useEffectEvent, correctly
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; splits the two jobs apart explicitly instead of hiding one of them:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ChatRoom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Always reads the CURRENT theme, no matter when this runs.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showNotification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Connected!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createConnection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// only roomId — and this time that's actually correct, not a lie&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome to &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key concept:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;onConnected&lt;/code&gt; is recreated on every render like any other local function, but calling it never reads a frozen snapshot — React always runs it against the component's latest props and state. Its identity is deliberately &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; stable across renders (unlike a &lt;code&gt;useState&lt;/code&gt; setter or a &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;-memoized function) — that's by design, so nothing can accidentally rely on it staying the same or pass it around like a normal callback. It simply can never legally appear in the dependency array in the first place, so the instability never causes a re-run. The Effect's dependency array now says something true: &lt;em&gt;this Effect only needs to re-run when &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; changes.&lt;/em&gt; &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; can change a thousand times without touching the connection, and the notification will still report whatever theme is active the instant it fires.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Toggle dark mode now: no disconnect, no reconnect, and the next notification shows the theme you just switched to. Both halves of the original bug — unwanted reconnects &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; stale reads — are gone, because they were never actually the same problem. They were two different values wearing one dependency array.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


🎮 Try it yourself
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://bestpractic.org/blog/react-weekly-useeffectevent-stale-closures/playground" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;▶️ Open the interactive playground →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Runs right in your browser — poke at it and watch the concept react live.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Stage 3 — more than one Effect Event
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The pattern scales past a single notification. Say the chat room also has a mute toggle that should silence a "ping" sound without, again, reconnecting:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ChatRoom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isMuted&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showNotification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Connected!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onMessage&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;((&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;isMuted&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;playSound&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;logMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createConnection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;message&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;msg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;onMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;msg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// roomId is the only reactive value here&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome to &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key concept:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;isMuted&lt;/code&gt; can each change independently, as often as the user likes, and neither one is a dependency anywhere. The rule that decides what goes in &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt;'s array hasn't changed — list every reactive value the Effect's &lt;em&gt;behavior&lt;/em&gt; depends on — it's just that &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;isMuted&lt;/code&gt; were never one of those to begin with. They were Effect Event inputs all along; &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; just gives that distinction a real API instead of a lint-rule workaround.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Edge cases and gotchas
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;You can only call an Effect Event from inside an Effect, or from inside another Effect Event.&lt;/strong&gt; Calling it during render, or handing it to a child component or another Hook as a prop, is not supported — &lt;code&gt;eslint-plugin-react-hooks&lt;/code&gt; (6.1 and later; the current major is 7.x) flags both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It must be declared at the top level of a component or custom Hook&lt;/strong&gt;, like any other Hook — not inside a loop, condition, or nested function. If you need one per item in a list, pull that item into its own component.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It cannot go in a dependency array.&lt;/strong&gt; You don't need to add it — the lint rule never asks you to — and if you add it anyway, a current &lt;code&gt;eslint-plugin-react-hooks&lt;/code&gt; flags it directly (&lt;code&gt;Functions returned from useEffectEvent must not be included in the dependency array&lt;/code&gt;) and tells you to remove it, because the whole point is that it isn't reactive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It is not a blanket fix for &lt;code&gt;exhaustive-deps&lt;/code&gt; warnings.&lt;/strong&gt; If a value genuinely should restart the Effect — &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; in every example above — wrapping it in &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; to make the warning go away reintroduces the exact stale-closure bug Stage 1 showed, just with a newer API wrapped around it. The question to ask every time is "should this value actually restart what the Effect is doing?", not "how do I make the warning stop."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It doesn't replace &lt;code&gt;useRef&lt;/code&gt; for everything.&lt;/strong&gt; If you need to read a value from &lt;em&gt;outside&lt;/em&gt; any Effect at all — say, inside a &lt;code&gt;setTimeout&lt;/code&gt; callback registered by an event handler, not an Effect — &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;'s restriction to Effects means a ref, or a plain callback prop, is still the right tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Server Components never run Effects&lt;/strong&gt;, so this is purely a client-component concern; it doesn't change anything about the server/client boundary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Best practices
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Reach for &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; when an Effect's trigger condition should stay narrow (one connection per &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt;) but an action it fires needs to use whatever is current at the moment it fires, not whatever was current when the Effect last started.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Don't reach for it reflexively&lt;/strong&gt; every time &lt;code&gt;exhaustive-deps&lt;/code&gt; complains. First ask whether the flagged value should actually resynchronize the Effect. If yes, keep it in the array — that's not friction, that's the rule doing its job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Keep Effect Events small and named for what they do&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;onConnected&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;onMessage&lt;/code&gt;), not for what they avoid (&lt;code&gt;stableTheme&lt;/code&gt;). The name should describe the moment it fires, because that's the mental model you're encoding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Pair it with a real connection/subscription pattern&lt;/strong&gt;, not a one-off side effect. The value of splitting reactive setup from non-reactive reaction shows up most in Effects that stay alive across renders — connections, subscriptions, timers — not in an Effect that runs once and is done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Is &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; a replacement for &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt;?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. &lt;code&gt;useCallback&lt;/code&gt; memoizes a function's &lt;em&gt;identity&lt;/em&gt; across renders so a child doesn't re-render or a dependency array doesn't see a "new" function every time. &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; doesn't memoize for performance — it changes what the function is &lt;em&gt;allowed to see&lt;/em&gt; (always-latest, never-reactive) and &lt;em&gt;where it can be called from&lt;/em&gt; (only Effects and other Effect Events). They solve different problems and aren't interchangeable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Can I call an Effect Event from a click handler?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No — an Effect Event can only be called from inside an Effect or another Effect Event, and the lint rule enforces this. If you need current-value behavior inside an &lt;code&gt;onClick&lt;/code&gt;, you already have it: a normal event handler always closes over the latest render's values naturally, because it's recreated every render. The stale-closure problem this Hook solves is specific to long-lived Effects, not short-lived event handlers.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Did this exist before React 19.2?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes, behind an unstable name. It shipped for a long stretch as &lt;code&gt;experimental_useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;, and the stabilized, unprefixed &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; landed in React 19.2 (October 2025). Code written against the experimental name needs the import updated, but the behavior and rules carried over.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Does &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; need a special ESLint setup?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You need a current &lt;code&gt;eslint-plugin-react-hooks&lt;/code&gt; (6.1+; 7.x as of this writing) for the linter to correctly exclude Effect Event functions from dependency-array warnings instead of flagging them as missing. Without it, you'll fight the linter over something it already knows how to handle in a current version.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What happens if I put the Effect Event function in the dependency array anyway?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A current &lt;code&gt;eslint-plugin-react-hooks&lt;/code&gt; flags it and tells you to remove it — it won't silently let it through. Functionally, adding it wouldn't do anything useful even if the linter allowed it: the function reference itself isn't what makes the behavior reactive or not. The reactivity question was never about the Effect Event's identity; it's about the values &lt;em&gt;inside&lt;/em&gt; it, which are intentionally not tracked.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Cheat sheet
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Situation&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;What to do&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Why&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A value decides &lt;em&gt;what&lt;/em&gt; the Effect connects to / sets up&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Keep it in the dependency array&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;It's reactive — the Effect's job changes when it changes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;A value is only read &lt;em&gt;after&lt;/em&gt; something the Effect set up fires&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Read it inside a &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Always current, never forces a re-run&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tempted to silence &lt;code&gt;exhaustive-deps&lt;/code&gt; by deleting a dependency&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Ask: should this value restart the Effect? If yes, keep it. If no, wrap the code that reads it in &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Deleting it silently reintroduces a stale closure&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Need current-value behavior inside an &lt;code&gt;onClick&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;onChange&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Do nothing special&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Event handlers already close over the latest render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Need current-value behavior inside a &lt;code&gt;setTimeout&lt;/code&gt; set up outside any Effect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Use a ref&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; only works from inside Effects&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;react&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;ChatRoom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;({&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;isMuted&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;})&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Non-reactive reads live here — never in the deps array, never the trigger.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;showNotification&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;Connected!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;});&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="c1"&gt;// Only truly reactive values live here.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;createConnection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;connected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="dl"&gt;"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;onConnected&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;());&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;connect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;()&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;connection&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;disconnect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;},&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]);&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;Welcome to &lt;span class="si"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;roomId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="si"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;h1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;&amp;gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


Key takeaways
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; dependency array lists &lt;strong&gt;reactive values the Effect's job depends on&lt;/strong&gt; — not every value the Effect's body happens to read.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deleting a value from the array to stop an unwanted re-run reintroduces a &lt;strong&gt;stale closure&lt;/strong&gt;: the deleted value gets frozen at whatever it was when the Effect last ran.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; (stable since React 19.2, October 2025) gives non-reactive reads a real home: the function always sees the latest props/state, but it's never a dependency and never retriggers the Effect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It can only be called from inside an Effect or another Effect Event — never during render, never passed to a child or another Hook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;It is not a workaround for &lt;code&gt;exhaustive-deps&lt;/code&gt; — if a value should genuinely resynchronize the Effect, it still belongs in the array.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


🧠 Test yourself
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think it clicked? &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://bestpractic.org/blog/react-weekly-useeffectevent-stale-closures/quiz" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Take the 8-question quiz →&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Instant feedback, a hint on every question, and an explanation for each answer — right or wrong.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That chat room from the opening scene now reconnects exactly when it should — when the room changes — and never when someone just prefers a darker screen. The bug was never really about dark mode; it was two different questions hiding inside one dependency array, and &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; is what finally lets you answer them separately.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If &lt;a href="https://dev.to/parsajiravand/react-derived-state-why-that-usestate-is-probably-a-bug-37h0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;React Derived State&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; taught you that an Effect syncing one piece of state into another is usually a bug, this is the companion lesson for the Effects you &lt;em&gt;do&lt;/em&gt; need: not every value they read is there for the same reason, and now there's a real API for telling them apart. And if &lt;a href="https://dev.to/parsajiravand/react-re-render-vs-remount-what-actually-triggers-each-5fok"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Re-render vs Remount&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; taught you that &lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt; decides which component instance you're looking at, the same instinct applies here — &lt;code&gt;roomId&lt;/code&gt; decides which &lt;em&gt;connection&lt;/em&gt; you're looking at, and &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; never should have.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Have you shipped a stale-closure bug from an Effect's dependency array — did you find it from a bug report, or from reading the code? Tell me below.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


📚 Read next
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/parsajiravand/react-derived-state-why-that-usestate-is-probably-a-bug-37h0"&gt;React Derived State: Why That useState Is Probably a Bug&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/parsajiravand/react-193-viewtransition-animate-state-without-losing-it-4kpp"&gt;React 19.3 ViewTransition: Animate State Without Losing It&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://dev.to/parsajiravand/react-re-render-vs-remount-what-actually-triggers-each-5fok"&gt;React Re-render vs Remount: What Actually Triggers Each&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




